@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100

### Public list: Aurora, Sentinel
GET {{baseUrl}}/Heroes

### Registered hero: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/Heroes/Details/2

### Draft hero: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/Heroes/Details/3

# ---------------- Web API (Demo 2) ----------------

### API: public registry, Registered heroes with their powers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes

### API: one hero in any status (Shadowling is a Draft)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/3

### API: unknown hero: 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/999

### API: invalid input: 400 before the action runs ([ApiController])
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": 99
}

### API: register a Draft without powers: 400 (a domain rule)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/3/register

### API: register a hero that is already Registered: 409 (the status)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/1/register

# ---------------- Minimal API (Demo 2): the same requests ----------------

### Minimal API: public registry
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes

### Minimal API: unknown hero: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes/999

### Minimal API: invalid input: 400 from ValidationFilter
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": 99
}

### Minimal API: register a hero that is already Registered: 409, same handler
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/minimal/heroes/1/register

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

# ---------------- Lab 2 ----------------
# Powers in the database: 1 Shield, 2 Light, 3 Flight.
# {{newHero.response.body.$.id}} is the id from the 201 response of the request named newHero.
# If your client doesn't support request variables, use that id directly.

### Create a Draft: 201 + Location
# @name newHero
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Nightwatch",
  "originStory": "A night guard who protects the old harbor district.",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Task 2: add Shield: 200, powers ["Shield"]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/powers/1

### Task 2: unknown power: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/powers/999

### Register: 200, status Registered
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/register

### Task 4: delete a Registered hero: 409
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}

### Task 3: retire: 200, status Retired
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/retire

### Task 3: retire again: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/retire

### Task 3: a Retired hero is read-only, add a power: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{newHero.response.body.$.id}}/powers/2

### Task 3: retire a Draft: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/3/retire

### Task 1: a Draft with a forbidden phrase: 201
# @name chosenOne
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codename": "Prophecy",
  "originStory": "The Chosen One of an ancient order of guardians.",
  "race": "Human",
  "alignment": "Heroic"
}

### Task 1: add Light: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{chosenOne.response.body.$.id}}/powers/2

### Task 1: register: 400, the story contains "chosen one"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{chosenOne.response.body.$.id}}/register

### Task 4: delete the Draft: 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{chosenOne.response.body.$.id}}

### Task 4: it is gone: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/heroes/{{chosenOne.response.body.$.id}}
